## 4. Implementation

### 4.1 Rust-to-Node Bridge (Dynamic Headless Identity)

`sleeve` is written in Rust; the Dynamic Node SDK is the fastest path to generating non-custodial Agent Identities without a browser. Use `src/cmd.rs` to execute an embedded Node script.

#### Node Bridge Script

`src/assets/agent-sandbox/dynamic_init.mjs`

```js
import { createDynamicClient } from '@dynamic-labs/sdk-node';

const environmentId = process.env.DYNAMIC_ENVIRONMENT_ID;
const machineId = process.argv[2]; // Passed from Rust

const dynamicClient = createDynamicClient({ environmentId });

async function initAgent() {
  const user = await dynamicClient.users.createOrUpdateUser({
    externalId: machineId,
  });

  const wallet = await dynamicClient.wallets.createEmbeddedWallet(user.id);

  console.log(JSON.stringify({
    address: wallet.address,
    dynamic_id: user.id
  }));
}

initAgent().catch(err => {
  console.error(err);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

#### Rust Subprocess Call

`src/cli/sleeves/identity.rs`

```rust
use crate::cmd::CmdLineRunner;
use machine_uid; // Add to Cargo.toml for stable hardware ID

pub fn initialize_agent_identity() -> eyre::Result<()> {
    let machine_id = machine_uid::get()?;

    let output = CmdLineRunner::new("node")
        .arg("src/assets/agent-sandbox/dynamic_init.mjs")
        .arg(machine_id)
        .env("DYNAMIC_ENVIRONMENT_ID", "your-id-here")
        .execute()?;

    // Parse output and store the 0x address in ~/.sleeve/agent.toml
    Ok(())
}
```

